        "body": "DeepCatch v2.3.0 — the open cfDNA fragmentomics benchmark.\n\n**What is in this release**\n- Held-out external validation on FinaleDB publications 1, 7 and 9, which\n  contribute no training data: AUC 0.9444 [0.8731, 1.0000] on one\n  whole-genome study (n=31), 0.708 [0.5148, 0.9012] on a second (n=52),\n  0.7385 [0.6281, 0.8488] pooled (n=83). No IRB and no data-use agreement:\n  the data are public and re-fetched by the scripts.\n- Leave-one-study-out transfer inside the training cohort (0.6805), so the\n  pooled figure is read as a within-cohort separation number, not a\n  generalisation claim.\n- A regularized late fusion (0.9825) and a Bayesian model average (0.9650)\n  replace the neural encoder (0.554) at this sample size.\n- The methylation channel runs end to end on real public fragments and is\n  reported as a null with its mechanism, not as a performance claim.\n- The submission PDF is attached: `biorxiv_submission_v2.3.0.pdf`.\n\n**Reproduce**\n    bash paper/REPRODUCE.sh\n\nEvery number in the manuscript is regenerated by the committed code from\nthe artifact committed in this repository.\n\nMIT licensed. Not clinically validated; research use only.\n",
